{"id": "section-body-01189", "title": "Headache", "chapterId": "chapter-one", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "The Concept of Emergency Care and Resuscitation", "Approach to Pain", "Headache"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-01189", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Headache", "runs": [{"text": "Headache"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1890"}}, {"id": "body-01190", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Normal", "text": "Approach to acute headache", "runs": [{"text": "Approach", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "to", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "acute", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "headache", "bold": true}]}, {"id": "body-01191", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Headache is a challenging complaint as it requires balancing symptomatic control with rapid assessment for life-threatening diagnoses. Headaches can be categorized into primary and secondary. Primary causes are neurologic and include tension, cluster and migraine. Secondary headaches are a result of an underlying pathological process such as malignancies, infections and other organic causes.", "runs": [{"text": "Headache is a challenging complaint as it requires balancing symptomatic control with rapid assessment for life-threatening diagnoses. Headaches can be categorized into primary and secondary. Primary causes are neurologic and include tension, cluster and migraine. Secondary headaches are a result of an underlying pathological process such as malignancies, infections and other organic causes."}]}, {"id": "body-01192", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Differential diagnoses", "runs": [{"text": "Differential"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "diagnoses"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-01194", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Sudden onset of severe headache", "runs": [{"text": "Sudden"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "onset"}, {"text":